{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":252849,"duration_api_ms":287772,"num_turns":36,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c88487d1-8454-424c-9a83-08e33a35c1c4","total_cost_usd":2.1344433,"usage":{"input_tokens":31,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78524,"cache_read_input_tokens":2334870,"output_tokens":7123,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78524,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":31,"outputTokens":7123,"cacheReadInputTokens":2334870,"cacheCreationInputTokens":78524,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.83644,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":77,"outputTokens":8920,"cacheReadInputTokens":886788,"cacheCreationInputTokens":131718,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2980033,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"evidence":["All acceptance criteria verified against source code: (1) Stage model distinguishes juvenile, sub_adult, adult StageCohorts (biology.rs:63-75, 130-182) with per-stage reserve_g, condition_index, maturation_accum; berried_females_count as adult-subset; egg_cohorts with per-cohort count/progress. (2) Lifecycle transitions are deterministic and one-way: juvenile_to_subadult (shrimp.rs:607-667), subadult_to_adult (shrimp.rs:670-731), spawning restricted to adults (shrimp.rs:424-427), egg_development resolves cohorts to juveniles (shrimp.rs:464-586). All use deterministic_transfer_count with signed carry. (3) Feeding is stage-weighted (1.0/0.67/0.3 at biology.rs:192-194) via feeding_units (biology.rs:507-511); mortality has per-stage sensitivity (shrimp.rs:749-758); all stages contribute to water chemistry via respiration/excretion/death-detritus routing. (4) Snapshot exposes total_shrimp_count, adult_shrimp_count, sub_adult_count, juveniles_count, berried_females_count (snapshot.rs:55-59); API BiologySnapshot mirrors these; TUI displays stage breakdown.","Invariant enforcement verified: enforce_invariants (invariants.rs:42-48) calls clamp_berried_to_adults(), reconcile_egg_cohort_counts() (new, biology.rs:602-621), and clamp_maturation_accum_to_count() on all three stages (biology.rs:125-127). validate_shrimp_runtime_params (invariants.rs:260-360) validates stage durations, condition thresholds, molt intervals.","Save migration verified: v4→v5 migration (save.rs:408-604) seeds juvenile_to_subadult_days/subadult_to_adult_days from legacy total maturation days via split_legacy_total_maturation_days (biology.rs:380-386). New StageCohort fields use serde(default) for backward compatibility.","Scenario materialization verified: shrimp_preset_to_params (tank_scenarios/lib.rs:546-600) wires stage-aware knobs with legacy fallback via apply_legacy_total_maturation_days.","Stage transition safety verified: receive_entrants (biology.rs:92-123) is used at all three transition points (shrimp.rs:538, 666, 730). Empty stages are re-seeded from incoming animals with maturation_accum=0 and condition from source stage. Non-empty stages do count-weighted condition blending.","clippy --workspace: clean, no warnings. fmt --all --check: clean (verified before cross-bead breakage).","New regression tests verified: hatch_into_empty_juvenile_resets_stale_stage_state (shrimp_population.rs:382-418) confirms empty juvenile stage is properly re-seeded; promotion_into_empty_subadult_resets_stale_stage_state (shrimp_population.rs:421-452) confirms empty sub-adult stage re-seeded; stage_model_conserves_population_counts_across_births_and_deaths (shrimp_population.rs:455-515) asserts total_count_change == births - deaths over 30-day run. All three assert deterministic values.","Pre-existing workspace compilation failure: algae_growth.rs references removed fields/functions (algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total, legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l) introduced by bead 6e5.7.1 (commit 45a0d83). Confirmed via git diff: bead 6e5.6.2 files are unchanged since its checkpoint (43902e4), and at that checkpoint algae_growth.rs had correct imports. This regression is fully outside this bead's scope."],"findings_or_gaps":["Cross-bead regression: bead 6e5.7.1 (commit 45a0d83) broke algae_growth.rs by removing legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l from imports and renaming ProcessParams fields (plant_half_saturation_n_mg_total → plant_half_saturation_n_mg_n_per_l) without updating algae_growth.rs which still references the old names. This prevents workspace-wide compilation and testing. Not attributable to 6e5.6.2.","The conservation test (shrimp_population.rs:455-515) isolates births and deaths by setting maturation days to 10000 (freezing promotions) and spawn_rate to 0 (no new berried). This is a valid targeted test but does not exercise the combined births+promotions+deaths accounting in a single run. The existing transition-specific tests cover individual promotion paths adequately.","The 60/40 juvenile/sub-adult split from legacy total maturation days is documented and has a clear override path, but no scenario preset currently specifies explicit stage durations, so all legacy scenarios use the inferred split."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Bead 6e5.7.1 must fix the algae_growth.rs compilation error before workspace tests can run again. The file references algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total, algae_half_saturation_p_mg_total, and legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l which were removed/renamed in that bead's process.rs changes.","Consider adding a combined-lifecycle conservation test that allows promotions, births, and deaths simultaneously over a multi-day run to catch potential inter-transition accounting errors. The current conservation test freezes promotions for isolation."],"outcome":"approved"},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0842f6ad-18fc-4f71-8884-fd74a2597d3e"}
